# FICTIONAL EXAMPLE — SQL Express installs as a named instance, breaking default-instance connection strings

> This is a fictional worked example of a knowledge entry, shipped with the template so you
> can see the shape. Real entries live at `knowledge/<area>/<slug>.md` — delete this file
> once you have written one.

**The claim, first.** SQL Server Express installs as the named instance `.\SQLEXPRESS`, not
the default instance. Every connection string that assumes `Server=localhost` fails with:

```
A network-related or instance-specific error occurred while establishing a connection to SQL Server.
(provider: Named Pipes Provider, error: 40 - Could not open a connection to SQL Server)
```

**The fix:** use `Server=localhost\SQLEXPRESS`, or reinstall choosing a default instance.

**Scope:** verified on SQL Server 2022 Express, Windows 11, default installer options.

Note the pattern this example demonstrates:

- the **title is a claim**, not a topic — it is what `qmd`/`rg` will match on;
- the **first paragraph is the answer**; evidence follows;
- the **verbatim error text** is included — future searches will be that exact string;
- the **scope is explicit** — versions and environment.
